# Ending: Strahd destroyed, and Ireena keeps the promise she made at the Pool of the White Sun (ireena_pool_choice is
# promised; data/endings/ireena_at_peace.json, ADR 0014). Ends with the sunrise of strahd_destroyed.

~ start
Narrator: The thing in the coffin goes still, and stays still. Far above you, stone groans, as if the whole castle has let out a breath.
Narrator: Three mornings later the sun is still rising, and Ireena asks to be taken to Krezk.
Narrator: At the Pool of the White Sun she kneels and looks into the water. The face that looks back at her is not her own.
Sergei: You kept your promise. So did I. I have waited a very long time.
Ireena: Then we will not make each other wait any longer.
if guest:ismark
Ismark: Go on, little sister. I will tell the village you were happy. It will even be true.
endif
Narrator: She steps into the pool, and the water takes the light and her with it. When the ripples settle, the surface shows only sky.
interject class:cleric: Wherever that light went, it was going home.
-> endings/strahd_destroyed:sunrise
